<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Houthi attacks and no Western support: What are Saudi Arabia's options ?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5af2e0c44e7cc5567fc30d0b7969b149bc3bfca53dd005ded96dd970080b6c87</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T12:24:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/houthi-attacks-and-no-western-support-what-are-saudi-arabia-s-options" /><summary type="html">The US has warned that fighting between Saudi Arabia and Iran-backed Houthis could rapidly escalate. It comes after a missile attack targeted Riyadh for the first time since the Yemen conflict resumed. The Houthis' lightning offensive seized swathes of Yemeni territory in recent weeks and has left hundreds dead. In the face of such attacks and with no support from its American ally, what are Saudi Arabia’s options?</summary></entry><entry><title>'NAZA' documentary about Gaza war sparks political storm in Israel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d7fa08580bad2c9c2ca309c1cf3709e1e6306a5433a0a24aa7213ab37f01e9f</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T12:22:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/naza-documentary-about-gaza-war-sparks-political-storm-in-israel" /><summary type="html">The Israeli filmmakers behind the documentary NAZA may have received a standing ovation at the Venice film festival, they have been facing violent threats to their lives and citizenship at home in Israel. A month ahead of crucial elections, the film profiles anonymous military sources who speak about the widespread killing of civilians in Gaza. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said he intends to introduce legislation aimed at revoking the citizenship of people who "defame IDF soldiers". Details by Shirli Sitbon, FRANCE 24 international affairs editor.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why doesn't the US intervene to defend Saudi Arabia against the Houthis?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7527cc6bf137486e4d8b36078fb006dde8b7fd1cb54320649f022df476d3ab15</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T12:20:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/why-doesn-t-the-us-intervene-to-defend-saudi-arabia-against-the-houthis" /><summary type="html">The US cautioned against a rapidly escalating situation in Yemen after Houthi rebels carried out a missile attack on the Saudi capital. In recent weeks, the Iran backed militants have also seized large portions of Yemeni territory following clashes with Saudi-backed government forces. The US is a very close ally to Saudi Arabia. Yet, is visibly unwilling to intervene on its behalf – why? Details and analysis by H. A. Hellyer, senior fellow in geopolitics at the Royal United Institute in Cairo.</summary></entry><entry><title>North Korea fires two ballistic missiles into the sea in latest weapons display</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44503b8e047b31932680e136ac9dd8ecdd4d48b43c381fbb3924df9da2a481b0</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T11:40:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260920-north-korea-fires-two-ballistic-missiles-into-the-sea-in-latest-weapons-display" /><summary type="html">North Korea fired two short-range ballistic missiles into the sea off its eastern coast on Sunday, South Korea’s military said. This came days after Pyongyang reaffirmed its status as a nuclear-armed state and rejected a UN resolution calling for an end to its nuclear activities.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Could regional polls force Friedrich Merz to step down?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f304023dd618b116628f0b550417343e45cddc63036077e1ec391b86b27106c</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T10:26:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/germany-could-regional-polls-froce-friedrich-merz-to-step-down" /><summary type="html">Polling is underway in the German capital Berlin and the largely rural state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania for regional elections. Both elections are seen as a test for Germany's centre-right Chancellor Friedrich Merz. He has already scheduled a crisis meeting and decided to skip this week's UN General Assembly to deal with the potential fallout. Could he be forced to step down based on the election’s results? Details and analysis by Yann Wernert, senior policy fellow at the Jacques Delors Centre in Berlin.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine hits Russia with major drone attack, targetting refinery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32aab22f83a686f70e97c987a3fe3d5f344f8674dd63777734b82991952deb60</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T10:24:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-hits-russia-with-major-drone-attack-targetting-refinery" /><summary type="html">In Russia, voters are on the third and final day of casting ballots in the country's first wartime parliamentary election. Despite the voting however, Ukraine carried out what Moscow described as the "largest ever" drone attack on the Russian capital. Kyiv reportedly fired over 1.000 drones at the country, leaving two dead in the Moscow region and inflicting damage upon an oil refinery. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Kyiv, Gulliver Cragg.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nine women found dead near Johannesburg sends shockwaves through South Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3c2d86ca04f2089dcc4fa83d221ab5dcde75f0ec9863699eb31ed8e39588c74</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T10:00:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nine-women-found-dead-near-johannesburg-sends-shockwaves-through-south-africa" /><summary type="html">Vigils, group runs and moments of silence: thousands of protesters gathered across South Africa this weekend to pay tribute to the nine women found murdered in eastern Johannesburg. In a country that records more than 60 homicides a day, the nine murders sent shockwaves through the population. Anger is mounting, and calls are growing for the government to take action. Story by Caroline Baum.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ed Sheeran calls Gaza war catastrophic after dropping Macklemore over pro-Palestinian comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9112b8c574d89e526616146514fbf3092b8d231ec64de8a544ce7a8b5791963</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:57:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ed-sheeran-calls-gaza-war-catastrophic-after-dropping-macklemore-over-pro-palestinian-comments" /><summary type="html">English singer Ed Sheeran opened his first show since his opener Macklemore was dropped after making pro-Palestinian comments onstage. The move sparked controversy and prompted several other support acts to drop out of the tour, publishing statements citing their support for Palestinians. While some concert goers could be seen trying to sell their tickets on Saturday, others have voiced their support for the 'Shape of You' singer. Story by Charlotte Hughes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Three media outlets barred from the White House over 'fake news'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba89e48f63b075fbff6210430b1fa010f4788e717aa232681abc7d8c7ca4eca0</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:55:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/three-media-outlets-barred-from-the-white-house-over-fake-news" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump has suggested that more news outlets may be barred from the White House after he announced he was banning Politico, CNN and MS NOW. On Saturday, all three outlets said that the White House confiscated their teams' press passes; they have also hinted at legal action. The ban has come under sharp criticism from press freedom advocates, as Charlotte Hughes explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>US and Denmark reach Greenland security deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6717d4806ef816f83c45f80f08e0d32ecc115f1740d84ed3863a7785738c19e</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:40:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-and-denmark-reach-greenland-security-deal" /><summary type="html">The US and Denmark have announced a deal on Greenland's security, resolving a diplomatic dispute sparked by President Donald Trump when he threatened to seize the semi-autonomous territory. The exact terms of the deal remain uncertain but it seems Denmark will maintain its sovereignty while the US will be able to develop a significant military presence on the island, and ban their adversaries from building their own bases on the island. Details by Charlotte Hughes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Houthis strike Saudi capital Riyadh for the first time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b09dfd9861e401f2ffa2156898d5cadb279935bd5b1922ff034904e1ad1b57b</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:38:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-strike-saudi-capital-riyadh-for-the-first-time" /><summary type="html">Fighting between Iran-backed Houthi rebels and Saudi Arabia continues to intensify. On Saturday morning, a fire broke out near Riyadh's main airport after Houthis said they launched missiles and drones at Saudi Arabia. On the ground in Yemen, Houthi rebels are pushing east in their fight against Saudi-backed government forces. Story by Caroline Baum.</summary></entry><entry><title>Argentines protest Milei's austerity, demanding higher wages and public spending</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45185d03d71db40d2c16e66c8ee706f11df8f6edaa0db3c81510025c816d1036</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:38:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/argentines-protest-milei-s-austerity-demanding-higher-wages-and-public-spending" /><summary type="html">Tensions are boiling over in Argentina, where a massive wave of public anger is spilling onto the streets of the capital. Following months of aggressive economic reforms and rising household debt, hundreds took to the streets in a "March of Anger", targeting President Javier Milei's austerity agenda. Details by Caitlin Brown.</summary></entry><entry><title>Will German's far right party AfD win over two more regions?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:405232f365d3fdbc56ec0050c601b044624136fd18ce8b0e28170b94504e053a</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:35:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/will-german-s-far-right-party-afd-win-over-two-more-regions" /><summary type="html">Two weeks after the far-right AfD won its first major regional election in Germany, two more eastern states vote this Sunday. Polls have just opened in the capital, Berlin, and the largely rural state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Berlin, Jörg Taszman.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ligue 1: Paris Saint-Germain head to Marseille for a tense Classique</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84e0ba6a3714706d20992c9ede982e2fb32aa8face85112b35ab9e3ed5dbc78d</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:34:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260920-ligue-1-paris-saint-germain-head-to-marseille-for-a-tense-classique" /><summary type="html">Paris Saint-Germain will travel to Marseille this Sunday to face OM at the Vélodrome in the final game of Matchday 5 in Ligue 1. It is a must-not-lose clash between two struggling sides, both looking to use this huge fixture to kick-start their seasons.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Russian election enters final day after major Ukrainian drone attack on Moscow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee20e13817285ff2605023d9a7224f7e3745ff177537c5dd356a3780463f15ee</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T07:10:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260920-live-russian-election-enters-final-day-in-shadow-of-war-in-ukraine" /></entry><entry><title>Live: Russian election enters final day after Kyiv targets Moscow in massive drone attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:794147824f37a76de5f4df2f492915f440b663b6c8e7a1a6553483611c0ecc68</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T05:16:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260920-live-russian-election-enters-final-day-in-shadow-of-war-in-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Ukraine launched what Moscow’s Mayor Sergei Sobyanin described on Sunday as the “largest ever” attack on the Russian capital, killing two people and damaging part of an oil refinery. The major attack comes on the third and final day of voting in Russia’s first wartime parliamentary election. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Merz under pressure as two more German states hold elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a8b061bc80799728b05491691c3f029d02ad57a99afa2b9bb49a31bf0338642</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T01:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260920-germans-vote-in-elections-threatening-fresh-blow-to-merz" /><summary type="html">Germans began voting Sunday in two closely watched state elections that could deliver fresh gains for the far-right and far-left, piling pressure on Chancellor Friedrich Merz as he struggles with low approval ratings and tensions within his governing coalition.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Pop, Protests &amp; Palestine: Ed Sheeran’s Moral Maze</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4847fa51d19fb90b3e935b096c8ba860598d2125fcefa7809f7a7f38c6e68778</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T21:49:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260919-pop-protests-palestine-ed-sheeran-s-moral-maze" /><summary type="html">A clash over music, politics and Palestine is putting freedom of expression in the spotlight. Macklemore’s outspoken support for Palestinians has sparked a backlash around Ed Sheeran’s US tour, raising a bigger question: should artists be expected to take a political stand, or are they equally free to stay silent? France 24’s Gavin Lee is joined by Dr Adam Behr, Reader in Music, Politics and Society at Newcastle University, to discuss the controversy.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>French police arrest two Germans after 'for fun' Louvre stunt in Mona Lisa hall</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe4637f5e1b4661231e83452c934264c495d65a97d1635c7e7056ac3a0faaf60</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T20:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260919-two-arrested-for-louvre-stunt-for-fun-in-mona-lisa-hall" /><summary type="html">Two Germans were arrested Saturday after they stuck two paintings on a wall of the hall that hosts the Mona Lisa in Paris's Louvre Museum, police sources said.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Macron and Carney to hold talks on strengthening Canada-France ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a79000c1f8773579b60722ed14413bd99f68a66d28c994740ed842f6f6edfeb</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T19:02:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260919-french-outpost-off-canada-in-the-spotlight-as-macron-hosts-carney-on-symbolic-visit" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron ⁠visited the French territory of Saint-Pierre-et-Miquelon on Sunday, where he will meet with Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney. The visit comes weeks after US President Donald Trump posted an image on social media showing the archipelago covered by the American flag.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Greenland Deal: Greenland: A Trump Win or Danish Masterclass?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85702695caf9df4a789830e960389ed64ac4d06004522e2fcb0103836b700920</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T17:37:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260919-greenland-deal-greenland-a-trump-win-or-danish-masterclass--49777f9c5bf2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260919-greenland-deal-greenland-a-trump-win-or-danish-masterclass" /><summary type="html">Is there a resolution on Greenland?
 
President Trump’s pressure campaign began in December 2024, right after he won re-election, when he began talking about the need for U.S. ownership and control of the semi-autonomous Danish territory.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>CNN, MS NOW, Politico reporters blocked from White House after Trump ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22266906c51caeb3d7daf731cf4708dfd4b1598b3bc8ec3808703124256bffad</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T17:02:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-cnn-ms-now-politico-reporters-blocked-from-white-house-after-trump-ban--a8c3f3f48609.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-cnn-ms-now-politico-reporters-blocked-from-white-house-after-trump-ban" /><summary type="html">White House correspondents for CNN, MS NOW and Politico on Saturday were blocked from entering the US president's office and residence a day after President Donald Trump announced he was banning the three media outlets for what he called "fake news" coverage. News organisations and press freedom groups have slammed the move as unconstitutional.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Germany braces for key state elections where far right party AfD seeks another breakthrough</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d6fe5f565a68b3edbbd5cf1418f408c6d362cfcb3674addbdf1a9a5ab653e59</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T15:28:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/germany-braces-for-key-state-elections-where-far-right-party-afd-seeks-another-breakthrough--ced0cb860143.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/germany-braces-for-key-state-elections-where-far-right-party-afd-seeks-another-breakthrough" /><summary type="html">Germany is gearing up for two more pivotal state elections on Sunday: in the capital Berlin and in the largely rural region of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania. All eyes are on the far-right AfD, which after recording its best ever result in the recent Saxony-Anhalt elections, is hoping to once again make sweeping gains. The anti-immigration party's surging popularity is proving challenging for Chancellor Friedrich Merz and both elections are expected to further test his leadership. Story by Eliza Herbert.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macron visits remote French territory in the North America, a first in over a decade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f66e2615c820677849c13b6d2accc944eb8dc9de9941b5e69c65831afecd09c</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T15:25:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/macron-visits-remote-french-territory-in-the-north-america-a-first-in-over-a-decade--a2f6eb83d168.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/macron-visits-remote-french-territory-in-the-north-america-a-first-in-over-a-decade" /><summary type="html">President Emmanuel Macron embarks on a rare and symbolic visit to a remote French territory in the North Atlantic on Saturday, hosting Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney at a time of growing tensions with Washington. The three-day visit to Saint Pierre and Miquelon, a three-island archipelago of under 6,000 people just off Newfoundland, will be the first by a French president in over a decade. Peter O'Brien tells us more about France's only remaining possession in North America.</summary></entry></feed>
